cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Time in range as a surrogate for HbA1c and for microvascular outcomes"
message: "If you use this software or data, please cite the article and this repository."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Rejaul
    family-names: Karim
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher"
  - given-names: Sumaeya
    family-names: Sultana
    affiliation: "Cheeloo College of Medicine, Shandong University, Jinan, China"
abstract: >-
  Analysis code and derived data for a two-stage meta-analysis of 21 randomised
  trials evaluating time in range as a trial-level surrogate for HbA1c, and a
  published-evidence surrogacy chain linking time in range to microvascular
  outcomes.
keywords:
  - continuous glucose monitoring
  - time in range
  - surrogate endpoint
  - meta-analysis
  - diabetes
